  "grid_coverage_explanation": [
    "The fixed highway design axis is north = east - 8 m. Alignment A rail design axis is north = -east - 8 m, while Alignment B is north = -east + 8 m.",
    "The rail design-axis intercepts differ by 16 m. The perpendicular distance between those adjacent diagonal railway positions is 16 / sqrt(2), approximately 11.313708499 m.",
    "Translating a crossing by one 16 m city-grid step both east and north keeps the highway design axis unchanged and changes the railway intercept by 32 m. The two supplied railway intercepts cover the two residue classes modulo 32 m.",
    "A half-turn reverses the upper-deck and lower-deck travel directions relative to the fixed highway; it therefore cannot replace the missing adjacent alignment while preserving that highway direction.",
    "Native GHSR chord endpoints contain 0.1 m asymmetries. Both alignments retain exact complementary native-helper boundary coordinates and tangents; design axes are not a substitute for those complete directed boundary checks."
  ],
  "limits": [
    "Software checks do not establish live construction, draggable continuation, Route Query, moving cars or trains, shadows, save/reload, or demolition.",
    "Two fixed owned cells occupy 2 by 1 tiles; four separate unowned helper cells require a clear 2 by 3 tile arrangement. Anchor padding is not an extra owned or helper tile.",
    "The train verification envelope is 5 m wide and 5 m high; it is a project bound, rather than a measured in-game automaton collision box.",
    "Proper object rotations and camera rotations are checked; mirrored placements remain outside this contract.",
    "No diamond assembly changes or runtime observations are included in this audit."
  ]
}
